 16│5. **Draft.** Stand where the Party stands and tell what reaches them in the order it would. Open on the situation: who is doing what, in a kind of place the listener can furnish for themselves. Danger leads when there is danger. Build toward the point around the anchor, under the craft rules, inside the length band, and end on the **reaction point**. Done when the block exists and its last sentence is the reaction point.
*17│6. **Revise.** Read the block aloud once and rewrite every sentence that snags. Pass the draft through the `humanizer` skill to strip AI tells, keeping every fact and every hard line below (it changes how the block reads, never what it says). Then run `pnpm cf narration <page> --callout "<title>" --band <min>-<max>` (with `--old <file>` holding the block you replaced): it counts words and sentences and finds echoes, banned punctuation, compass words, foot counts, list-like runs and judgement words. Rewri...
 18│7. **File.** Replace the callout's body and keep its title. Run `pnpm check <page>` until it passes.
